      "id": "US-05.2",
      "title": "Ask the spouse's nationality, permit and residence only when they can exempt the employee",
      "as_a": "hr",
      "i_want": "the questionnaire to ask a married employee for the spouse's nationality, permit and country of residence, but only when the employee would otherwise be subject to source tax",
      "so_that": "I no longer have to check the spouse exemption by hand and chase the spouse details by email, and no spouse data is collected when it cannot change the outcome",
      "priority": "P1",
      "priority_reason": "HR checks the spouse exemption by hand today and asks for the spouse details by email, which 'takes forever'. Getting it wrong sends the source tax questions to the wrong people.",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        {
          "id": "AC-05.2.1",
          "title": "Spouse's nationality is asked only of married employees who would otherwise be subject",
          "given": "the employee has given their home country, nationality, permit (if asked) and civil status (asked in the family step)",
          "when": "the employee is \"Married\", lives in Switzerland, is not Swiss and does not hold a C permit",
